<h2>Scope and operator</h2>
<p>This Privacy Policy applies only to Daily Breath, operated by Beyond Imagination Technology. It covers the Daily Breath website and installed web app, Apple app and extensions, and Android app distributed through supported stores. Other Beyond products have separate notices. Beyond ID is used only when you choose account-connected features and is also governed by its own account privacy notice.</p>

<h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
<p>You may provide reflection journal text, scripture notes and highlights, favorite collections, breathing and challenge activity, Academy progress, chat questions, support messages, and newsletter details. Some of this information can reveal personal wellness or religious interests. Please do not place medical records, passwords, payment-card numbers, or information you are not authorized to share in notes, journals, support requests, or chat.</p>

<h2>Trivia answers and scores</h2>
<p>Daily Breath uses your trivia answers only to calculate and display your result for the current quiz session. The web version processes answers during the current request, and the Apple app keeps quiz progress in memory while you play. Daily Breath does not save general trivia answers or scores to your Beyond ID, create a trivia leaderboard, or use trivia responses for advertising.</p>

<h2>Beyond ID and account-connected features</h2>
<p>Most reading and local practice features can be used without an account. If you sign in with Beyond ID, Daily Breath receives or uses an account identifier, name, email address, authorization token, connected-app status, and the minimum account information needed to authenticate you, restore eligible purchases, sync supported progress, prevent abuse, and provide support. Native authorization tokens are stored in the platform’s protected credential storage. You may sign out from the app or manage account data through Beyond ID.</p>

<h2>Web app data</h2>
<p>The web app may store language, tradition, theme, accessibility settings, notes, highlights, favorites, and installation preferences in your browser. When you intentionally save a web reflection, breathing session, challenge result, Academy entitlement, or Academy progress while signed in, Daily Breath stores the relevant record with your Beyond ID. Reflection text is encrypted before database storage. Newsletter signup stores the name and email address you submit until you unsubscribe or request deletion.</p>

<h2>Apple app data and optional iCloud sync</h2>
<p>The Apple app stores journal entries, scripture notes, highlights, favorite collections, challenge progress, breathing history, daily history, language, tradition, and appearance preferences in protected local app storage. If you explicitly enable Encrypted iCloud Sync, the app encrypts supported private data on your device before placing it in your Apple iCloud key-value store; the encryption key uses iCloud Keychain. Beyond Imagination Technology does not receive the unencrypted journal or scripture-note content through that sync feature. Widgets and the App Clip receive only the content and settings needed for their displayed experience.</p>

<h2>Android app data</h2>
<p>The Android app stores journal entries, selected tradition, language, breathing progress, and other local preferences in private on-device app storage. Android backup is disabled for the app. Choosing Share opens the Android system share sheet and sends only the reflection text you choose to the app or recipient you select. The app requests internet access for sign-in, chat, content refresh, purchase restoration, and other account-connected features; it does not request contacts, precise location, camera, microphone, or broad file access.</p>

<h2>Daily Breath chat</h2>
<p>When you send a message to Chris, Dovi, or Moe, the message and recent chat context are transmitted over HTTPS to Daily Breath’s server so it can return app help or a sacred-text response. Daily Breath chat is restricted to Daily Breath and sacred-text topics and uses a local, no-GPU response service. It does not send Daily Breath prompts to a third-party generative-AI provider. Conversation history is kept in the current app or browser session and is not intentionally stored as a reusable server-side chat transcript. Limited security, rate-limit, and server logs may be retained temporarily to operate and protect the service.</p>

<h2>Purchases</h2>
<p>Academy purchases may be processed by Apple, Google Play, Amazon, or Stripe, depending on platform. Those providers process payment credentials under their own privacy policies. Daily Breath receives limited purchase information such as product, store or customer identifier, transaction status, entitlement status, refund or cancellation status, and timestamps so it can grant, restore, protect, and support access. We do not intentionally store full payment-card numbers on Daily Breath servers.</p>

<h2>Diagnostics and first-party analytics</h2>
<p>The native apps do not include advertising SDKs or cross-app tracking. The web app may use first-party visitor analytics to understand reliability and usage, including page, time, device category, operating system, browser family, viewport, language, timezone, referring domain, country code, and limited network-derived information. Visitor and session identifiers are protected with one-way hashing; URL query strings and full browser user-agent strings are not retained. Browser Do Not Track signals are respected.</p>

<h2>How information is used</h2>
<p>We use information to deliver requested readings and practices, authenticate accounts, provide chat responses, save or sync selected progress, process and restore purchases, send requested newsletters or service messages, answer support requests, secure the service, prevent abuse, diagnose failures, meet legal obligations, and improve Daily Breath. We do not sell personal information or use Daily Breath data for cross-context behavioral advertising.</p>

<h2>Service providers and disclosures</h2>
<p>Information may be processed by hosting, email, security, payment, app-store, and cloud-platform providers only as needed to operate the features you use. Apple processes optional iCloud data; Apple, Google, Amazon, or Stripe process applicable purchases. We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect users or the service, or as part of a business transaction with appropriate notice and safeguards. Providers receiving user data are required to protect it consistently with this policy and applicable law.</p>

<h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Local app and browser data remains until you delete it, clear app or browser storage, or uninstall the app. Turning off iCloud sync leaves the local copy intact; iCloud copies are controlled through your Apple account and supported app controls. Account-linked records are kept while needed to provide the feature and for security, accounting, dispute, purchase-restoration, and legal obligations. Newsletter details remain until unsubscribe or deletion. Security logs are retained only as reasonably necessary for protection and troubleshooting.</p>
<p>You may delete local reflections and notes using available app controls or platform storage controls. The <a href="/dailybreath/data-controls.php">Data &amp; Account Controls page</a> explains how to remove local data and request access, correction, export, or deletion of account-linked Daily Breath data. We may need to verify your identity. Purchase records may be retained where required for tax, fraud-prevention, or transaction obligations.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures, including HTTPS, protected platform credential storage, access controls, encrypted sensitive records where described, rate limiting, and restricted administrative access. No storage or transmission method is completely secure.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Daily Breath is a general-audience faith and wellness app and is not directed to children under 13. Beyond ID and account-connected features should not be used by a child without authorization from a parent or guardian where required. Contact us if you believe a child submitted personal information without appropriate consent.</p>

<h2>International use and your rights</h2>
<p>Information may be processed in the United States and other locations where our service providers operate. Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, or obtain a copy of personal information, or to withdraw consent for optional processing. We will respond as required by applicable law.</p>

<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
<p>We may update this policy when Daily Breath’s features or legal obligations change. We will update the effective date and provide additional notice when required. Questions or privacy requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:support@beyond-os.com?subject=Daily%20Breath%20privacy%20request">support@beyond-os.com</a>.</p>

<p class="legal-note"><strong>Store disclosures:</strong> App Store privacy answers and Google Play Data safety declarations must remain consistent with the behavior described here and must be updated whenever Daily Breath’s data practices change.</p>
